nodes.body:
I understand this PR is still a work in progress, but just wanted to share that I noticed that if system messages are structured with an array in the following form in non 0th indexes, they'd still fail the validation for LLMs that require the system message to only be at the 0th message.

```
[
      {
        'role': 'system', 
        'content': 
            [
                {
                    'text': "My initial system message for the LLM,
                    'type': 'text'
                }
            ]
        }, 
        {
            'role': 'user', 
            'content': [
                {
                    'text': 'some input from the user ', 
                    'type': 'text'
                }
            ]
        }, 
        {
            'role': 'system', 
            'content': [
                {
                    'text': 'Injected system prompt later in the convo', 
                    'type': 'text'
                }
            ]
        }
]
```

